DVT Licensing Terms

1. Base License

DVT core software ("DVT Core") is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public
License, version 3 ("AGPLv3"). The complete, unmodified text of the AGPLv3 is in
the LICENSE file distributed with DVT.

For purposes of these terms, DVT Core means the DVT software distributed under
the AGPLv3, excluding separately licensed third-party components and software
that qualifies as a DVT Extension under these terms.

The DVT Extension Exception below is an additional permission under section 7
of the AGPLv3. It does not replace the AGPLv3 or waive its requirements for DVT
Core.

2. DVT Extension Exception

The copyright holders of DVT Core grant the following additional permission:
software that qualifies as a DVT Extension may interact with, be loaded by, be
combined with, and be distributed with DVT Core through the Documented DVT
Extension Interfaces without the terms of the AGPLv3 applying to that DVT
Extension solely because of that interaction, loading, combination, or
co-distribution.

This exception applies only to the extent stated in these terms.

3. What Qualifies as a DVT Extension

A "DVT Extension" is a separate work designed to add functionality to DVT Core
through one or more Documented DVT Extension Interfaces.

"Documented DVT Extension Interfaces" means extension points that DVT project
documentation identifies as officially supported interfaces for extensions.
They include, as applicable, the DVT Extension manifest, the public DVT
Extension API, extension node registration, extension Gateway entrypoints and
routes, extension migration and database facilities, and other officially
documented extension interfaces that DVT may provide in the future.

A work is not disqualified from being a DVT Extension merely because it is
installed together with DVT Core, distributed in the same package or delivery,
loaded or executed by DVT Core, or runs in the same process as DVT Core.

4. What the Exception Permits

A qualifying DVT Extension may be licensed under terms chosen by its copyright
holder, including Open Source, proprietary, or commercial terms. It may be
used, modified, sold, licensed, and distributed separately from DVT Core or
together with DVT Core.

A qualifying DVT Extension may, through the Documented DVT Extension
Interfaces, register nodes, add Gateway routes using the supported extension
mechanism, use supported extension migration and database facilities, and use
other officially supported extension capabilities.

Using the Documented DVT Extension Interfaces by itself does not require an
otherwise independent DVT Extension to be licensed under the AGPLv3 or require
its source code to be made available under the AGPLv3 solely because of that
use.

5. What the Exception Does Not Permit

This exception is a narrow compatibility permission. It does not grant an
exception from the AGPLv3 for DVT Core itself or for code to the extent that it:

- copies or incorporates substantial portions of DVT Core source code;
- modifies DVT Core;
- is based on DVT Core for reasons other than its use of the Documented DVT
  Extension Interfaces;
- incorporates or embeds DVT Core internal implementation instead of using the
  Documented DVT Extension Interfaces; or
- distributes a modified version of DVT Core.

This exception does not state that access to DVT internals is technically
prevented or sandboxed. Use of interfaces that are not Documented DVT Extension
Interfaces receives no additional permission under this exception; the AGPLv3
and applicable copyright law continue to govern such use.

Nothing in this exception changes the legal test for whether a work is a
modified work, covered work, or other work based on DVT Core, except for the
specific additional permission granted above.

6. Bundling, Distribution, and Modified DVT Core

Distributing or installing DVT Core together with a qualifying DVT Extension
does not, by itself, change the license of that DVT Extension. DVT Core remains
licensed under the AGPLv3, and recipients retain all rights in DVT Core granted
to them by the AGPLv3.

Bundling may not be used to avoid the AGPLv3 requirements for DVT Core. A
modified version of DVT Core remains subject to the AGPLv3, including the
corresponding source requirements that apply when the modified DVT Core is
conveyed.

7. Network Use

This exception does not waive or limit section 13 of the AGPLv3 for DVT Core.
If modified DVT Core is made available for users to interact with remotely
through a computer network, the source-code obligations of the AGPLv3 continue
to apply to DVT Core as provided by that license.

8. No Trademark Grant

Neither the AGPLv3 nor this DVT Extension Exception grants rights to use any
project or company name, trademark, service mark, or logo, except to the extent
such use is permitted or required by applicable law.
